== Photoelectric effect
When light strikes surfce of certain metals, electrons are ejected. $e^-$ are called photoelectrons
- Quantum theory used by Einstein (1905) to explain the Photoelectric Effect.
  - Shining a beam of light is shooting beams of particles, or *photons*, at the metal atoms.
  - Light behaves as a stream os massless particle, *photons*.
  - $E = h*v$ is the energy of a single photon

